comment.narrative:
•Three (3) investigations conducted including one on SGBV and one involving children rights and one vulnerable group’s rights;
•Four (4) follow-up investigations conducted in Naivasha; Laikipia; Meru and Bomet;
•Recommendations on appropriate resolution mechanisms of the investigated complaints made.

•353 complaints were processed across the KNCHR regions;
•252 of those complaints were by male complainants while 90 were by females and 1 related to intersex person;
•Twenty-Three complaints (7%) of the total complaints received were by or relating to rights of PWDs;
•2 Strategic partners engagement forums held with partners in Nakuru and Garissa;
•Two (2) Joint public complaints handling initiatives held in Elgeyo Marakwet and Meru;
•140 complaints received and processed towards resolution.
•Debriefing session for HQ staff; North Eastern Regional Office Staff and the Central Regional Office staff.

•One (1) consultative workshop with Teachers Service Commission (TSC) representatives on the rights of intersex children and adults in Kenya;
•Advocacy and Public awareness forums in Nakuru, Kisii; Taita Taveta; Wajir; and Marsabit Counties;
•Finalization of Global Citizenship Education Research Report-Focus on Rights of Intersex Children.
